# Without this file, Git's core.autocrlf=true (common on Windows) rewrites
# LF bytes to CRLF inside these files too, since Git has no other way to know
# they aren't text. For binary formats that silently corrupts them - caught
# 2026-09-27 when a merge produced a resume.pdf that grew by 115 bytes and
# failed to parse (mismatched xref table). Marking them binary here stops
# Git from touching their bytes at all.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
